.55}, {"uuid": "dc8c1d18-3976-48c0-bdf1-f9bcb999cdd4", "regime": "small", "axes": {"total_q": 92, "len_indptr": 6}, "correct": true, "speedup": 31.96}], "geomean_speedup": 11.93, "arithmetic_mean_speedup": 15.06, "min_speedup": 7.36, "max_speedup": 44.08, "decision": "keep", "cumulative_evaluations": 4, "skills_used": ["KernelWiki"], "notes": "New best (marginal): geomean 11.71->11.93x (+0.22), 21/21 correct. num_stages=3 confirmed helps the compute-bound cases as hypothesized: #5 31.54->34.36, #6 33.44->36.42, #20 29.48->31.55, #17 42.80->44.08, #4 (81 tok) 14.57->15.15. Tiny/micro cases ~neutral in speedup (8.2-8.55x; note absolute sol time rose ~0.049->0.056ms but ref also rose this run => cross-run timing noise; the tiny speedup ratio held, so no real regression). Net geomean up because the large-case gains outweigh tiny noise. Decaying returns continue (c002->c003 +1.44, c003->c004 +0.22). Geomean is tiny-dominated (17/21 near their ~0.05ms launch floor), so further large-case tuning yields <=~0.2 geomean per step. Remaining branch-A knobs: num_stages=4 (likely smem-limited at BLOCK_M=128,BLOCK_N=64,D=128 -> may not compile/help), BLOCK_N=128 (fewer loop iters, more work/iter on large cases), num_warps=4 (may reduce tiny-case launch cost). Next candidate c005: BLOCK_N=64->128 to halve KV-loop trip count on large cases (more wgmma per iter, better pipeline amortization); guard tiny cases (single tile => neutral) and smem (K+V bf16 tiles [128,128] ~64KB, fits Hopper 228KB). Next parent: c004."}
